<BaseLayout title="Network — Onuros" description="Onuros network design: shielded payments, GPU proof of work, measurable performance, and development-network status.">
  <section class="page-hero"><p class="kicker">Network</p><h1 class="display">Built to be measured.</h1><p class="lead">Onuros combines a C++ blockchain core, privacy components written in Rust, and explicit activation gates for performance, recovery, and security.</p></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="eyebrow-line"><p class="kicker">Design commitments</p></div><div class="rule-list"><div class="rule-row"><span>01</span><div><h3>Private transfers</h3><p>Sender, receiver, and amount are designed to remain concealed on-chain.</p></div></div><div class="rule-row"><span>02</span><div><h3>GPU proof of work</h3><p>Accessible mining paths for AMD and NVIDIA hardware with node-side verification.</p></div></div><div class="rule-row"><span>03</span><div><h3>Evidence-backed gates</h3><p>Performance, recovery, and adversarial testing must pass before readiness claims.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="eyebrow-line"><p class="kicker">Performance</p></div><div class="split"><h2 class="section-title">100 private TPS is a measured development target.</h2><div><p class="copy">The goal is sustained private transaction processing across multiple nodes on published hardware. Confirmation time, transaction size, relay performance, and storage impact are measured separately.</p><p class="copy">A development result is not a promise of future mainnet capacity.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
